      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The Adios 9 has a low-stack, minimalist setup (about 27-28 mm heel and 20-21 mm forefoot, 7 mm drop) that feels soft underfoot from Lightstrike Pro but still gives strong ground feel and less impact protection than max-cushioned options.",
        "Responsiveness: The full Lightstrike Pro midsole is described as very energetic with quick energy return, feeling lively and flexible, and especially strong for tempo and interval sessions.",
        "Stability: A midfoot stiffening/plastic element is used to add torsional rigidity and guide forefoot flex, while the upper and lacing provide secure lateral hold; heel structure is less rigid because there is no traditional plastic heel counter.",
        "Durability: The outsole was redesigned to mostly Lighttraxion with a small Continental rubber section; traction/grip is praised, but the provided text does not give a clear long-term outsole wear or material longevity result."
      ]
    }
